WEBVTT

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.760
Lady Marrine.
Word is that Lord Alexis has been attacked.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.510
What did you say?

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.760
However, he apparently
suffered no injuries, and is now safe.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.970
That so?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.230
The details are still unclear,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.480
but it seems he was caught
in the crosshairs of some Union in-fighting.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.320
So it wasn't the people
behind my father's assassination?

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.790
Alexis!

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.210
Why now, after the incident in the Great Hall?

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.590
Lord Alexis has expressed his desire to speak
with you, no matter what it takes.

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.130
Why don't you consider hearing him out?

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.220
Father's assassination
was a premeditated plot.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:05.810
Those who were against our marriage
triggered that tragedy.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:08.770
My lady...

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.990
We were never meant to
be together, that's all!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.960
I see.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.300
To plot an assassination
is a bold move for Lord Pederico.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.430
Still...

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.390
Just as I suspected, the marquis
is still in love with Marrine, eh?

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.560
It did seem that way.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:11.480
Do you two know how
the marquis and Marrine first met?

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.310
No.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.440
All I've heard is that they met
while studying in Eramu.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:20.410
Right. That's where they fell in love,
six years ago.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.710
What's going on?

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.460
There's a man sitting in the middle of the road.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.960
Judging by his outfit,
I'd say the son of a Lord.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.220
This is a public carriage road.
Kindly abstain from such reckless behavior.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.480
The cobblestones used to pave
this road are so very beautiful.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:52.770
Reflecting the sunlight, sparkling and lovely!

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.820
My name is Alexis.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.910
My name is Marrine.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.790
I've known the word "love".

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.630
But after seeing you,
for the first time, I now know what it means!

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.130
Is that your favorite pick-up line?

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.690
My lady, a letter has arrived for you.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.860
Is it from that young man again?

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.030
- Please put it away.
- Very well.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:47.780
Perhaps you could read just one,
and decline his advances in a letter?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.660
I suppose.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.840
Right now, I am enveloped in
the joy of discovering what love is.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:10.720
That is what moves me.
Tonight, I will deliver flowers to you.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.390
Tonight?

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.600
Does that mean a messenger
will be arriving shortly?

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.080
Are those roses?

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:34.330
Last night, Lord Alexis appeared,
saying he'd come to bring you flowers,

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:36.880
and then suddenly started
lining up those stones.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.710
I see.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.710
Well, he's a bit odd, but interesting, yes?

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.550
Do you think I'll need to thank him for this?

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:52.810
Lord Alexis often attends soirées
where the sons of Lords gather, I'm told.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.740
Well, well! You're a new face here.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.700
Your hair is lovely.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:18.500
Your hips are so slender,
I'm dying to put my arms around them!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:25.920
Would you mind not touching me?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.890
I have no interest in you whatsoever.

00:06:28.890 --> 00:06:30.180
H-How dare you!

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.310
Let's stop.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.150
<i>Alexis?</i>

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.900
This young lady doesn't want your attention.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.940
You mustn't try to force yourself on her.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.610
Listen, you! Stay out of my business!

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.620
Lord Alexis!

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.270
How do you feel?

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:26.030
Am I dreaming, perhaps?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.400
This isn't a dream.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:30.700
Your wound must hurt.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.120
Now that we've met again, I'm certain.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:40.580
You're Jalucia's Prince of the Sun,
Alexis, aren't you?

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.790
And I know who you are, too.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:48.210
But still, why did you come to this soirée?

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:52.640
You gave me such lovely flowers,
so I wanted to thank you.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:58.730
You knew about my family,
so why did you fall in love with me?

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.900
In Eramu, family names mean nothing.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:06.570
When I met you, my heart skipped a beat,

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.230
and I realized it was love.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:11.740
That's all there is to it.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.950
But you and I are enemies
who can never be united.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:20.500
That may be true, but I can't resist
a heart that now knows love.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:23.750
I could sense how you felt
just by reading your letters.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.500
It was like reading the script
of a romantic play!

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:32.260
But... it's a play that will end in tragedy.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.860
This is my thanks for the flowers.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.860
It's my first kiss ever.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.160
Not that you have to treasure it...

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:59.910
Let's end this right now,
as I have no intention of seeing you again.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.710
If that's what you want...

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:06.710
But I will never forget you.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.590
Because all that you are
is now inscribed in my soul.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:36.700
I thought we were heading
to Lord Darcy's mansion?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.870
My lady, please look outside.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.000
Let's do it again, one last time! Ready?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.330
Okay!

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:48.460
Three, two...

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:52.920
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star...</i>

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:57.340
<i>How I wonder what you are...</i>

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.510
What were you thinking?

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:57.340
I am prepared to be rebuked.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.770
<i>Up above the world so high...</i>

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:03.520
It's just... I could no longer bear
seeing you so crushed.

00:10:01.770 --> 00:10:06.190
<i>Like a diamond in the sky...</i>

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.310
I'd call that unsolicited concern!

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:10.650
We're not very far
from where Lord Alexis lives.

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:10.650
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star...</i>

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:15.780
<i>How I wonder what you are...</i>

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:15.780
He's been known to come here by foot,
and interact with the children like that.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:17.280
Right! Well done!

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:21.160
All right, everyone,
now take your silver coins, and head on home.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.790
Okay!

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.120
- Here.
- Thanks!

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.040
Here.

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.920
Is that his idea of interacting?

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:33.050
Bye, Alexis!

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:46.980
You do realize
that you'll lead the Union one day?

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.770
And yet here you are,
handing out silver coins to children.

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.150
Perhaps it gives you satisfaction...

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:57.450
But if you start giving charity to some,
there will inequity.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.530
And it will gradually
undermine your sovereignty.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.870
You may be right about that.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:06.870
But I don't see what I'm doing as charity.

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:12.000
At first, they only did it
for the money I gave them.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.800
But that's not how it is now.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:17.380
Now they look forward to singing together.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:19.470
What do you mean?

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.300
Charity is the act of giving
money or things, nothing more.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:27.730
The recipient may feel gratitude,
but there's no joy.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:31.980
For someone to live in bliss,
their heart must be filled.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:34.820
But that is not a Lord's duty.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.990
I don't see it that way.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:40.990
Rather, I think it to be
the most important thing of all.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:45.490
If a sovereign has forgotten that,
he'll eventually bring his people grief.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.370
That's not possible.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.200
That's...

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.540
...just an ideal.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:54.210
Even if attaining that ideal is an arduous path,

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:58.510
as long as you keep pursuing it,
you can certainly get closer!

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:03.350
Why is it you're able to say that
with such conviction?

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.520
Because those children smile
when they're with me now.

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.020
A sovereign who fills people's hearts...

00:12:23.780 --> 00:12:25.580
I've made up my mind.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:38.800
What have you decided?

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.050
I'll be your queen.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:47.560
It seems I have fallen in love with you as well,
so it can't be helped.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:50.060
I don't know how long it will take.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:53.600
But I promise to come for you.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.070
So don't ever have a change of heart,
and wait for me.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:58.070
Marrine!

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:03.280
Of course I'll wait for you!
And I would never have a change of heart!

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.570
Because no one but you can fill my heart!

00:13:14.330 --> 00:13:17.340
That's what I know
of how their romance began.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:21.510
I would've been against a political marriage.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:25.640
But if they truly love one another,
they should be together.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.850
No matter who they are.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:41.440
Then we agree, Pederico Rossini's penalty
will be expulsion from the Union?

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:42.570
No objection!

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:47.120
All right, next on the agenda
is Lord Dawson's proposal.

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.740
I find the Earl of Altirk's actions
to be highly questionable!

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:57.710
Since you took it upon yourself to
go to war against the Factory Alliance,

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:01.670
a truce no longer looks likely,
and the Union is in crisis!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:02.960
I see.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.380
Regarding the circumstances
behind that battle,

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:10.390
I'll have my vassal, Theo Cornaro,
explain it all to you.

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:11.560
Huh?

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:13.220
Right.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:18.770
I've repeatedly sought the allegiance
of Lord Pavel of Starck,

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.400
but have yet to receive an answer.
What's the meaning of this?

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:27.160
Allegiance cannot be for form's sake.
There must also be an emotional connection.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:29.740
It is not something so easily pledged.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:34.250
Meaning he can't recognize
someone of my caliber as his master?

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.500
What he means is that he cannot at this time.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:40.790
Should you show him
that you are equipped to lead the Alliance,

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.300
my Lord will feel assured.

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:46.010
So he's telling me to
first prove that I'm equipped?

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:51.260
If you're seeking my Lord's allegiance
at this time, that's what he wishes you to do.

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:57.270
That is all.

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:03.940
The crucial point is that the battle Theo set off
wasn't against the Alliance.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:07.610
Banishing a Lord who'd run afoul
of the court rank system,

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.990
and seizing his court rank and lands
was a justified action.

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:13.660
Isn't that right, mages in attendance?

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:24.670
And then, it was the Alliance
who launched an attack on Theo Cornaro.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:29.300
Surely you aren't suggesting
he not fight back under enemy attack?

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:33.430
Announcing himself as a member of the Union
while surrounded by Alliance forces...

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:36.310
It's no wonder he was attacked.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.100
In other words,

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:42.020
it's no wonder my Altirk
came under Alliance attack, doesn't it?

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:44.360
I never said that!

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.820
Stop twisting my words!

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:48.950
Lord Dawson, please calm yourself.

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:54.330
I admit that it was the Alliance
who set off the battle.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.490
But if you hadn't lent a helping hand,

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:59.460
our relationship with the Alliance
wouldn't have soured.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:04.090
Until the moment Waldlind intervened,
that might've been the case...

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:10.130
But Waldlind rejected Theo Cornaro
when he sought to join the Alliance,

00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:12.010
and sent their knights after him.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:15.720
That's the reason why he requested my aid.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:18.180
You should've just ignored him!

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.730
It was your arbitrary decision
which set off that battle with the Alliance!

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.440
- That's right!
- Don't try to rationalize it!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.150
I should've just ignored him?

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:34.950
I love the Fantasia Union,
which prizes freedom and peace.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:39.660
For that reason, I want to protect
anyone who joins the Union.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:45.340
If any one of you here came under attack,
I guarantee that I will come to your aid.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:52.800
By the way,
the small, neutral continent of Bredland,

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.680
is about to be attacked by the Sea King Erik.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.060
Considering the Union as a whole...

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.730
...the only option is to thwart him.

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.190
I couldn't agree more.

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:09.230
Should we be denounced for having
protected Sievis, now part of the Union?

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:14.990
My astute fellow Lords, please consider
the overall interests of the Union.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.910
<i>This is the clincher.</i>

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:22.080
<i>Now this conference
is under Sir Villar's control.</i>

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.830
I now know where you all stand.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.960
We, the Fantasia Union, will confront
the Factory Alliance with military might.

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:31.630
Does everyone agree?

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:33.680
Yes, I see no problem.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:34.800
No objection.

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.390
No objection...

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.520
Personally, I'd rather not
go to war with the Alliance.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.640
Of course, I'll comply with today's decision.

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:48.230
However, there's one thing
I'd like to propose, if I may.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:54.650
I only became your leader
because my father was an Archduke.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:18:00.790
And now I think we should choose the man
who's best-suited to lead the Union.

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:07.000
Now that we've decided to
take on the Alliance in battle,

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:12.380
I believe no one is more suited to be leader
of the Union than the Earl of Altirk.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:16.760
And if the Earl of Altirk
does become our leader,

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:20.810
I intend to be the first to offer
my services to him.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.150
Is this the birth of Archduke Villar Constance?

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:30.020
No.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.400
I lose this time.

00:18:33.030 --> 00:18:34.400
What do you mean by that?

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:35.570
It's obvious.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.410
Although I'm honored by
your endorsement, Lord Alexis,

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.540
I respectfully decline.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:47.330
And that's because...

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:55.760
I doubt my grandfather, Jurgen Kreische,
would want to see his grandchildren fighting.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:01.680
<i>That's right...</i>

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:07.100
<i>It was Jurgen Kreische, the Blood-and-Iron Earl,
who founded the Factory Alliance.</i>

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.150
<i>The Fantasia Union was created to counter it.</i>

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:18.030
<i>And half of the blood running
in Lord Villar's veins is Kreische blood.</i>

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:26.410
I believe that the Marquis of Jalucia
is the best man to lead the Union, after all.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.750
No objection!

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:31.170
And since we've chosen
the Marquis of Jalucia as our leader,

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.960
I believe we should
pursue peace talks with the Alliance.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:37.720
The Alliance will never accept peace.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:41.300
They'll bolster their forces,
and we'll soon be under attack, without fail!

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.560
Are you sure you still want to proceed?

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.850
Sir, are you going
to defy the will of our leader?

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.480
I haven't acknowledged this yet.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:52.110
Then would you like to
become leader yourself?

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:59.740
All right, once again,
does anyone object to peace?

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:01.740
No objections!

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:16.380
<i>The Union has squandered
a golden opportunity to destroy the Alliance.</i>

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:21.090
<i>This time around, Waldlind is sure to
attack the Union with their pride at stake.</i>

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:24.510
<i>Will Altirk be able to withstand it?</i>

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:32.150
A messenger from the Union
has proposed peace.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.360
What did you say?

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:39.150
First Sievis, and if that wasn't enough
they seize Forbes and Clovis,

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:40.900
and now they seek peace?

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:42.780
I don't blame you for being angry,

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:48.290
but the Union wishes to follow the agenda
agreed upon before the Great Hall Tragedy.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.960
The agenda under which
I'd marry the Marquis of Jalucia,

00:20:50.960 --> 00:20:53.420
uniting the families of the two Archdukes?

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:54.420
Yes.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.210
That seems to be the will of Alexis Doucet,
leader of the Union.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:05.850
I want you to tell Gerhart
to prepare for battle with Starck.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.720
He likely has no intention of serving me.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:10.810
I'll be taking part as well.

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:16.060
We'll use the conquest of Starck
as a foothold to invade Altirk.

00:21:17.070 --> 00:21:17.900
Understood.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:56.150
Goodbye, Alexis...

